Package: noisyvalue
Title: Analyze Differentially Private Data with Honest Uncertainty
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Steven", "Baldasty", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "sbaldasty@gmail.com")
Description: Tools for analyzing data released under differential privacy,
    such as the 2020 Census noisy measurement files. Each released number
    is a noisy value: the observed figure together with a posterior
    distribution over the true value it measures. Noisy values work in
    tibbles and support arithmetic, credible intervals, and probabilities
    of comparisons (for example, how likely one count is to exceed
    another), with the uncertainty from the privacy noise carried through
    every calculation.
License: MIT
Encoding: UTF-8
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Depends: R (>= 4.1)
Imports:
